<mjml>
  <mj-head>
    <mj-font name="Source Sans Pro" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Source+Sans+Pro:200,400,700&display=swap" />

    <!-- defines the style for different tags -->
    <mj-style inline="inline">
      a {
        color: #fbc926; /* Make links this color */
      }
      p {
        margin: 0.2em 0; /* Adjusts vertical spacing */
      }
      h2 {
        text-decoration: underline; /* Adds underline */ margin-bottom: 0.1em; /* Adjust margin below */ color: #ffffff
      }
    </mj-style>
  </mj-head>

  <!-- defines the color of the background that the column of content sits on top of -->
  <mj-body background-color="#222">
    <!-- add an empty section for padding at the top of the email -->
    <mj-section> </mj-section>

    <!--  defines the background color behind the text -->
    <mj-section padding="0" background-color="#000000">
      <mj-column>
        <!-- insert a banner image -->
        <mj-image padding="0" width="600px" src="https://static.presidentscup.us/2025.11.18.game-of-the-month-banner.png" alt="2026 President's Cup Competition Banner. #PRESCUP" />

        <!-- defines the text style (font and color) -->
        <mj-text font-family="Source Sans Pro, sans-serif" padding-top="20px" font-size="16px" color="#ffffff" line-height="1.3">
          <!-- insert email content here -->
          <p>
            <span>Hello,</span>
          </p>
          </br>

          <p>
            <span>The President's Cup Cybersecurity Competition team challenges you to test exploitation and cyber operations skills in this month’s </span>
            <span><a href="https://presidentscup.cisa.gov/game-of-the-month/">Game of the Month</a><b>: "Discounted Route to Rescue"</b> (PC5, R1).</span>
            <span>This challenge will push you to analyze target architecture, exploit vulnerabilities, and strengthen your offensive cyber tradecraft.</span>
          </p>
          <br />

          <p>
            <span>📌 <a href="https://www.cyber.mil/dod-workforce-innovation-directorate/dod-cyber-workforce-framework">DoD Cyber Workforce Framework</a> Roles:</span><br />
            <ul>
              <li>Cyberspace Operator (CE-322)</li>
              <li>Exploitation Analyst (CE-121)</li>
            </ul>
            <span>📌 <b>DCWF Tasks covered:</b></span><br />
            <ul>
              <li><b>2020A</b>: Analyze target operational architecture for ways to gain access.</li>
              <li><b>2029A</b>: Apply and utilize authorized cyber capabilities to enable access to targeted networks.</li>
              <li><b>2660</b>: Conduct cyber activities to degrade/ remove information resident in computers and computer networks.</li>
              <li><b>2119</b>: Conduct network scouting and vulnerability analyses of systems within a network.</li>
            </ul>
            <span>🔗 <b>Gameboard Link:</b> [<a href="https://pccc.cisa.gov/gb/practice/065b0dc83a2b4bcb8ec017e887d3bb6d/discounted-route-to-rescue">Practice - Discounted Route to Rescue</a>] 
          </p>
          <br />

          <p>
            <span><b>Why Participate?</b></span><br />
            <ul>
              <li><b>Develop Key Cybersecurity Skills</b> - Practice real-world exploitation techniques, container breakout, and privilege escalation.</li>
              <li><b>Boost Your Career </b> - Strengthen skills aligned with Cyber Operator and Exploitation Analyst roles.</li>
              <li><b>Challenge Yourself </b> - Navigate a compromised ship, break into restricted services, and recover mission-critical data.</li>
            </ul>
          </p>
          <br />

          <p>
            <span>🔹 <b>Competition Stats:</b></span><br />
            <span>✅ <b>Solvability Rate</b>: Full: 22% / Partial: 21%</span><br />
          </p>
          <br />

          <p>
            <span>Join the challenge today and put your expertise to the test! </span>
            <span>If you have any questions about the Game of the Month Challenge, please email the <a href="mailto:PresidentsCup <presidentscup@cisa.dhs.gov>">President's Cup Team</a>.</h3>
          </p>
          <br />

          <p>
            <span>Federal employees looking to enhance their cyber skills can visit the <a href="https://pccc.cisa.gov/gb/practice">Practice Area</a> to tackle past PC challenges and earn completion certificates for continuing education credits.</span>
            <span>The <a href="https://github.com/cisagov/prescup-challenges">President's Cup GitHub</a> is another great way to access artifacts, solution guides, and additional resources from previous competitions.</span>
          </p>

        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- add an empty section for padding at the bottom of the email -->
    <mj-section> </mj-section>
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
